{"abstract":"Three dimers of the amphipathic α-helical peptide 18A have been synthesized with different interhelical linkers inserted between the two copies of 18A. The dimeric peptides were denoted 'beltides' where Beltide-1 refers to the 18A-dimer without a linker, Beltide-2 is the 18A-dimer with proline (Pro) as a linker and Beltide-3 is the 18A-dimer linked by two glycines (Gly-Gly). The self-assembly of the beltides with the phospholipid DMPC was studied with and without the incorporated membrane protein bacteriorhodopsin (bR) through a combination of coarse-grained MD simulations, size-exclusion chromatography (SEC), circular dichroism (CD) spectroscopy, small-angle scattering (SAS), static light scattering (SLS) and UV-Vis spectroscopy. For all three beltides, MD and combined small-angle X-ray and -neutron scattering were consistent with a disc structure composed by a phospholipid bilayer surrounded by a belt of peptides and with a total disc diameter of approximately 10 nm. CD confirmed that all three beltides were α-helical in the free form and with DMPC. However, as shown by SEC the different interhelical linkers clearly led to different properties of the beltides. Beltide-3, with the Gly-Gly linker, was very adaptable such that peptide nanodiscs could be formed for a broad range of different peptide to lipid stoichiometries and therefore also possible disc-sizes. On the other hand, both Beltide-2 with the Pro linker and Beltide-1 without a linker were less adaptable and would only form discs of certain peptide to lipid stoichiometries. SLS revealed that the structural stability of the formed peptide nanodiscs was also highly affected by the linkers and it was found that Beltide-1 gave more stable discs than the other two beltides. With respect to membrane protein stabilization, each of the three beltides in combination with DMPC stabilizes the seven-helix transmembrane protein bacteriorhodopsin significantly better than the detergent octyl glucoside, but no significant difference was observed between the three beltides. We conclude that adaptability, size, and structural stability can be tuned by changing the interhelical linker while maintaining the properties of the discs with respect to membrane protein stabilization.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Andreas Haahr","Sørensen, Kasper Kildegaard","Johansen, Nicolai Tidemand","Martel, Anne","Kirkensgaard, Jacob Judas Kain","Jensen, Knud Jørgen","Arleth, Lise","Midtgaard, Søren Roi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-508357"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institut Laue-Langevin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dimeric peptides with three different linkers self assemble with phospholipids to form peptide nanodiscs that stabilize membrane proteins","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-508357","identifier":[{"id":"84978120440","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27306692","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c09540eb-6494-40bf-b8e6-1656f1443e28"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F7819A0D4E55174BB6CA32FA952D936C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Xray and Neutron Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"institut laue langevin","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institut Laue-Langevin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas Nørgård","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6c4e1152-e925-4026-9178-46d90be8db31","name":"Larsen, Andreas Haahr","name_org":"Larsen, Andreas Nørgård","orcid":"0000-0002-2230-2654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper Kildegaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"fe952500-0336-4f5e-a97f-cf2097fc3e0d","name":"Sørensen, Kasper Kildegaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai Tidemand","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"82ee2df4-1f0f-43c2-bf9e-65ed6e56abd4","name":"Johansen, Nicolai Tidemand","orcid":"0000-0002-8596-548X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne","key":"martelpau","last":"Martel","name":"Martel, Anne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob Judas Kain","key":"kirkensgaardpau","last":"Kirkensgaard","locid":"50870496-8308-49f5-87ba-200a5a3dc051","name":"Kirkensgaard, Jacob Judas Kain","orcid":"0000-0001-6265-0314","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Knud Jørgen","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"816e7a29-7615-4a4e-bfd2-f98150c116ab","name":"Jensen, Knud Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0003-3525-5452","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise","key":"arlethpau","last":"Arleth","locid":"15d83378-85d7-49d2-a442-242f57f46967","name":"Arleth, Lise","orcid":"0000-0002-4694-4299","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Roi","key":"midtgaardpau","last":"Midtgaard","locid":"af8c25d3-54a3-485c-9afd-0c3d6da84a6f","name":"Midtgaard, Søren Roi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27306692"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c6sm00495d","issn":["09599428","1744683X"],"issn_org":["1744683X"],"issue":"27","journal":"Soft Matter","pages":"5937-5949","status":"p","title":"Soft Matter","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978120440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c09540eb-6494-40bf-b8e6-1656f1443e28"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dimeric peptides with three different linkers self-assemble with phospholipids to form peptide nanodiscs that stabilize membrane proteins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-508357","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Within the field of pen needle development, most research on needle design revolves around mechanical tensile testing and patient statements. Only little has been published on the actual biological skin response to needle insertions. The objective of this study was to develop a computational method to quantify tissue trauma based on skin bleeding and immune response. Method: Two common sized pen needles of 28G (0.36mm) and 32G (0.23mm) were inserted into skin of sedated LYD pigs prior to termination. Four pigs were included and a total of 32 randomized needle insertions were conducted. The affected tissue was removed and fixated in formalin following tissue preparation for histology. Standard immunohistochemical staining procedure was applied with CD-45 and anti-hemoglobin primary antibodies to stain immune cells and red blood cells, respectively. The stained tissue slides were subsequently digitized using 200X magnification. Based on thresholding, morphological masks and blob detection, segmentation of the histology was performed to locate tissue bleeding and immune response. Image-to-image registration was used on images originating from the same tissue, and a quantitative measure of tissue trauma was obtained for each needle insertion. Result: Bleeding and immune response were seen for all tested needles. Positive correlation was seen between the needle diameter and the size of the bleeding. The quantitative measure reveal a trend that tissue trauma decreases with decreasing needle diameter. Conclusion: A computational and quantitative method has been developed to assess tissue trauma following insulin pen needle insertions. Application of the method is tested by conduction of a needle diameter study. The obtained quantitative measures of tissue trauma correlate positively to needle diameter.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jensen, Casper Bo","Larsen, Rasmus","Vestergaard, Jacob Schack","Conradsen, Knut","Kildegaard, Jonas","Præstmark, Kezia Ann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-368610"],"event":{"end":"2013-11-02","place":"San Francisco, California, us","start":"2013-10-31","title":"13th Annual Diabetes Technology Meeting","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantification of tissue trauma following insulin pen needle insertions in skin","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/81745710/prod11389264853227.Jensen13.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-368610","ids":["dtu-d65cbdd3-6a2f-4948-a346-94b16191846a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-16CAAC475601B9EBE9490AD1C40C83D6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/81745710/prod11389264853227.Jensen13.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper Bo","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Casper Bo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b3ea098f-fc7a-48a0-